<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Charroux</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">989</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charroux">Charroux</a> was a church synod held in 989 at the abbey of Charroux in Poitou, convened by Archbishop Gunbald of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bordeaux">Bordeaux</a>. Its canons threatened excommunication for anyone who robbed churches, attacked unarmed clergy or seized the livestock of peasants and the poor. It is usually seen as the beginning of the Peace of God, a movement of councils that sought to limit aristocratic violence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p></div>
